{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd","id":1534441,"title":"Is World of Darkness is a bit more of a power fantasy than CofD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-19T08:40:24-07:00","id":1534441,"title":"Is World of Darkness is a bit more of a power fantasy than CofD?","content":"I've readed some of people opinion on WoD, and it seem that the setting seem to be much more on the power fantasy side than CofD, but is this how the game is represented?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T09:13:36-07:00","id":1534443,"title":"","content":"WoD games other than Vampire are generally concerned with something else, which makes any question of power levels require some heavy re-contextualization. Most characters that are doing military stuff in a military game are generally going to be using materiel that's a good deal more potent than what's in the hands of a random survivalist hunter, whether you're talking about a game of Power Armor in Cyberpunk 2020, a game with a BattleTech RPG in the Deep Periphery with no major state assistance vs one closer to the Succession Wars, or the difference between Forsaken and Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T09:29:12-07:00","id":1534444,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t really think of Werewolf the Apocalypse (or any of the WoD games) as a military game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T16:28:43-07:00","id":1534467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1534444#post1534444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t really think of Werewolf the Apocalypse (or any of the WoD games) as a military game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their game's monster status is literally Rank, and they engage in open, armed conflicts in locales like the Amazon, where the art presents them openly toting assault rifles most of the time. Their law also has specific precepts about what is and isn't allowed in an open time of war. It's hard to get more explicit on the subject of &quot;this is a game about war&quot;, but that's mostly because they don't do a lot of far past historical games about when the Garou had the greater numbers to engage in actions that weren't mostly guerilla warfare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T17:49:58-07:00","id":1534469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd#post1534441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've readed some of people opinion on WoD, and it seem that the setting seem to be much more on the power fantasy side than CofD, but is this how the game is represented?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not how the games are represented... but it is side effect of how the games are as a total product.<br /> <br /> The intent of the WoD is for the PCs to feel powerful - they are monsters and all - but for the costs to ultimately outweigh the positives to make it something that doesn't qualify as &quot;power fantasy&quot; and instead wants to be an urban fantasy game with powerful characters in it. But the implementation of that has been... spotty over the decades. So the WoD is very easy to play as a power fantasy for people that want to do that, even if that's not what the books were aiming for.<br /> <br /> One of the whole reasons behind some of the changes in the CofD and why it was originally meant to replace the WoD, was to &quot;fix&quot; that. To make the downsides of being a supernatural sting more so the game didn't slide into power fantasy as easily. There were of course costs to that, which a lot of people didn't think were worth it even if they didn't want to play the WoD as a power fantasy either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-21T22:07:16-07:00","id":1534540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1534469#post1534469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not how the games are represented... but it is side effect of how the games are as a total product.<br /> <br /> The intent of the WoD is for the PCs to feel powerful - they are monsters and all - but for the costs to ultimately outweigh the positives to make it something that doesn't qualify as &quot;power fantasy&quot; and instead wants to be an urban fantasy game with powerful characters in it. But the implementation of that has been... spotty over the decades. So the WoD is very easy to play as a power fantasy for people that want to do that, even if that's not what the books were aiming for.<br /> <br /> One of the whole reasons behind some of the changes in the CofD and why it was originally meant to replace the WoD, was to &quot;fix&quot; that. To make the downsides of being a supernatural sting more so the game didn't slide into power fantasy as easily. There were of course costs to that, which a lot of people didn't think were worth it even if they didn't want to play the WoD as a power fantasy either.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, not all of the games were really oriented towards personal horror. Mummy is probably the most notable example of this, but it was apparent as early as Mage 2e. Ascension is focused around philosophical warfare and the search for transcendence. There is the difficulty of Seekings, the threat of Quiets, and the terror of realizing one's power, of course, but by default, the game does not really frame mages as monsters. If anything, the game presents mages quite positively. Even in 1e, most of the conflict is external. <br /> <br /> In any case, you are right in that the structure of the OWoD games often renders them something of a power fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T09:10:23-07:00","id":1534647,"title":"","content":"There is nothing wrong with power fantasy. And if the ST of the chronicle does not want it to be directed toward that general schema of play, they can easily do so.<br /> <br /> The overexaggerated angst against &quot;power fantasy&quot; is the reason why cWoD is.. the way it is, in regards to all currently released 5th edition titles nowadays. And the way it is now isn't good at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T09:57:00-07:00","id":1534699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1534540#post1534540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, not all of the games were really oriented towards personal horror. Mummy is probably the most notable example of this, but it was apparent as early as Mage 2e. Ascension is focused around philosophical warfare and the search for transcendence. There is the difficulty of Seekings, the threat of Quiets, and the terror of realizing one's power, of course, but by default, the game does not really frame mages as monsters. If anything, the game presents mages quite positively. Even in 1e, most of the conflict is external.<br /> <br /> In any case, you are right in that the structure of the OWoD games often renders them something of a power fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually not even Werewolf is oriented towards personal horror, despite having doses of it, but that is besides the point.<br /> <br /> The games were intended mostly for Urban Fantasy, horror or not, but as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, the whole package ended up being quite easy to &quot;devolve&quot; into power fantasy. Which isn't a problem in itself.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Mages are definitely monsters, they violate reality and everything people rely on, with the goal of making their own personal visions become true by force. The game not being about angst with that doesn't make them good guys in the end, regardless of their belief on the contrary.<br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness has a far firmer grasp on being Urban Fantasy without Power Fantasy, in this regard it is a greater success, but...<br /> <br /> Well, you can actually go either way with either setting. The only problem you may have is if the group as a whole wants to avoid Power Fantasy, but one player in particular is a power gamer asshole (in opposition to a power gamer that is nice and civil). Only in this very particular situation would I say CofD is a better option to reign in the problem player without being an asshole in turn.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, it is more that each game is its own thing than being more or less whatever you measures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T11:04:55-07:00","id":1534705,"title":"","content":"Chronicles of Darkness reaches higher power level. In fact one of the few things i don\u00b4t like about it is how abusing rules can lead to dice inflation.<ul><li>CoD archmages belong to a Higher Plane of Reality existing outside of it in their golden roads a</li> <li>The GodMachine is basically a demiurge</li> <li>Fae are alien beings who operate under a contractual reality.</li> <li>Spirits of High ranks can compete with Archmages</li> <li>Vampires are way more powerful in Requiem than in masquerade. Blood Potency can give +30 to physical stats, disciplines are also stronger and way more versatile. Requiem has rules for antediluvian level powers in a way that they are playable. We literally have stuff that can compete with EndGame Tzimisce from Gehena like the Eyeless Mother which is a living discipline.</li> <li>Etc..</li> </ul>People think masquerade is stronger because they only saw the first books hard restart and assumed everything stayed street level.<br /> <br /> The thing with CoD is that it has tiers from street level (TIER 1) to cosmic level (TIER 4) which allows players to customize how they want to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 04-25-2024, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T11:30:40-07:00","id":1534708,"title":"","content":"The problem is most of the examples of &quot;high power level&quot; listed are either things PCs can only achieve after a lot of play (as many have in-game requirements beyond just earning enough XP and many of those requirements are in the ST's hands), or are NPC only material.<br /> <br /> The issue with the WoD vs the CofD here, is that the WoD can easily accidentally slide into power fantasy without meaning to because you happen to go down the right mechanical path. CofD requires you to be more purposeful if you want to go there (this isn't a bad thing, there's a published 1e CofD book with a whole ton of optional rules in it all about amped up power levels of the PCs in it).<br /> <br /> Power fantasy isn't really about the relative power of entities in different settings because it's the power within the setting that makes it a power fantasy.<br /> <br /> You can have a power fantasy in a zombie apocalypse where the PCs are all technically humans, even if somehow the ragtag group of survivors are also the most skilled badasses in the world that easily mow down the undead, rebuild society, and so on. The fantasy is the ability to exercise power that IRL you don't have. In video games, there are games where you're playing a normal human soldier that has to be careful because one stray bullet could end a mission as they're &quot;realistically&quot; fragile (they're not when it comes to stabilizing and healing damage, but they make the threat of death a lot higher before that can happen) that are fun in their own way, and there are video games where you're playing a &quot;normal human&quot; soldier that makes Captain America look like a punk as they take on mecha-Hitler and all his goons by himself. Wolfenstein is also fun, but it's certainly a lot more power fantasy than most of the WWII set Call of Duty games are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T18:39:48-07:00","id":1534787,"title":"","content":"High end CofD is cosmic level, and players have a lot of control on what they're doing. Not only that, a starting Vampire in CofD is undoubtedly more powerful in general than a starting Vampire in WoD.<br /> <br /> <b>Unless </b>we have a good starting combo.<br /> <br /> And that's the thing. With CofD, the Storyteller has an easier time keeping the power level within whatever constraints they want. Which doubles as a better time keeping the relative power between PCs and NPCs, which is the real point.<br /> <br /> The question in the end boils down to how much can the PCs exercise power over the setting without facing serious consequences, that is what a power fantasy is.<br /> <br /> WoD has a lot of ways you can amass far more power in practice than you should by design, and a big part of this is access to do things with starting or low XP characters that completely undermine the expected power of NPCs.<br /> <br /> But again, that may be a problem in some groups, or for inexperienced Narrators. But as long as everyone plays in good faith, it is simple to avoid traps, or correct course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T12:54:04-07:00","id":1535297,"title":"","content":"It's presented as a horror setting with each setting working on a different part of the genre. With Vampires it's a personal horror as you see your humanity slip further and further away and you start having problems with plots that could endanger people and even people you might care &quot;about&quot; and your not really bothered by it anymore. I can't speak with werewolves and what they touch and with Mages you got a group of people who could rewrite reality on a whim and upset what you hold as true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T20:37:55-07:00","id":1535329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1534540#post1534540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, not all of the games were really oriented towards personal horror. Mummy is probably the most notable example of this, but it was apparent as early as Mage 2e. Ascension is focused around philosophical warfare and the search for transcendence. There is the difficulty of Seekings, the threat of Quiets, and the terror of realizing one's power, of course, but by default, the game does not really frame mages as monsters. If anything, the game presents mages quite positively. Even in 1e, most of the conflict is external.<br /> <br /> In any case, you are right in that the structure of the OWoD games often renders them something of a power fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was about to say that. Mages are the heroes of their own stories. They are NOT monsters AT ALL. In fact, they are basically &quot;Super Humans&quot;. And indeed, they are humans, fully humans, from head to tail. Humans with super powers. &quot;Uber Humans&quot;. They are the best and brightest humanity has to offer. Mage is very, very far away from the entirety &quot;oh, I am a monstrous monster living in the shadows&quot;. There's none of that in Mage, unless you have that fetish for being so. But then you'll just be a weirdo, not a &quot;typical&quot; Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 05-08-2024, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-09T10:41:36-07:00","id":1535360,"title":"","content":"The Garou are the heroes of their own stories too... though I doubt any of us real humans playing the game would want to live under Garou rule.<br /> <br /> The fact that mages aren't physically different from humans (inherently) doesn't make them not monsters. The same reason having super-powers don't make you a hero. It just makes you a person with power other people don't have. <i>The Boys</i> is all about &quot;super-humans&quot; how just how much they can be monsters whether they're as powerful as Homelander, or just as uncaring about morality in the pursuit of stopping Homelander as Butcher.<br /> <br /> Mage is all about illustrating that being human doesn't make you immune from being a monster; especially when you're handed powers beyond human comprehension. Powers that are not handed out to the &quot;best and brightest&quot; but seemingly randomly (maybe once upon a time to the best at the brightest, but that system was broken long ago if it actually existed)<br /> <br /> The fact that Mage isn't about &quot;personal angst&quot; like Vampire is doesn't mean it isn't about deeply broken people that do horrible things while painting themselves as the morally correct type of mage an other mages on a spectrum of ignorant to evil. It's almost like I didn't even use the phrase &quot;personal horror,&quot; in the post Verlan was responding to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-09T13:24:41-07:00","id":1535365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1535360#post1535360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Garou are the heroes of their own stories too... though I doubt any of us real humans playing the game would want to live under Garou rule.<br /> <br /> The fact that mages aren't physically different from humans (inherently) doesn't make them not monsters. The same reason having super-powers don't make you a hero. It just makes you a person with power other people don't have. <i>The Boys</i> is all about &quot;super-humans&quot; how just how much they can be monsters whether they're as powerful as Homelander, or just as uncaring about morality in the pursuit of stopping Homelander as Butcher.<br /> <br /> Mage is all about illustrating that being human doesn't make you immune from being a monster; especially when you're handed powers beyond human comprehension. Powers that are not handed out to the &quot;best and brightest&quot; but seemingly randomly (maybe once upon a time to the best at the brightest, but that system was broken long ago if it actually existed)<br /> <br /> The fact that Mage isn't about &quot;personal angst&quot; like Vampire is doesn't mean it isn't about deeply broken people that do horrible things while painting themselves as the morally correct type of mage an other mages on a spectrum of ignorant to evil. It's almost like I didn't even use the phrase &quot;personal horror,&quot; in the post Verlan was responding to.</div> </div> </div> </div>An examination of the dangers of powers and hubris is certainly something that is possible in Mage. The game, however, does not adhere entirely to that framework. If anything, each reader is intended to come away from Mage with their own interpretation as mages. To say that mages are unequivocally monsters is like saying that miracle-workers throughout history were monster. Even apart from ethical considerations, it is just a myopic way of viewing the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-09T14:10:24-07:00","id":1535368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1535365#post1535365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An examination of the dangers of powers and hubris is certainly something that is possible in Mage. The game, however, does not adhere entirely to that framework. If anything, each reader is intended to come away from Mage with their own interpretation as mages. To say that mages are unequivocally monsters is like saying that miracle-workers throughout history were monster. Even apart from ethical considerations, it is just a myopic way of viewing the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Book of Secrets is but one of many books where the author directly states it: make no mistake, Mages are monsters.<br /> <br /> What happens is that the game, as all other games in WoD, has many themes to explore, and angst about your own monstrosity isn't the main one by far.<br /> <br /> Angst for being a monster isn't particularly important (but still possible) in any line but Vampire. Yet Werewolves take lives almost as an afterthought, fairies are emotional vampires at best and serial kidnappers with some frequency, your best Demon is a cult leader with all that entails. They're monster, inevitably, all of them.<br /> <br /> Mages aren't simply enacting miracles. They're raping reality with the stated goal of making it what they think it should be, without any concern for what other people want or need it to be.<br /> <br /> They bend and break rules, abuse minds and destinies, they trash around as they see fit. And the common people can't do shit about it, they're stripped of any right to interject or adequately resist, they're robbed of any sense of safety on even the most basic expectations on how the very reality around them should work.<br /> <br /> It is true to the game even if it isn't a focus or theme, which is another thing entirely. You shouldn't play Mage ruminating how despicable your nature is. But while your character may never see it that way, they're monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-09T14:15:04-07:00","id":1535370,"title":"","content":"I think all the WoD playable creature types are monsters. That being said, I\u2019ve never seen a group play WoD as a power fantasy, but maybe that\u2019s just because I\u2019ve been lucky with the groups I\u2019ve played with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-09T14:31:23-07:00","id":1535373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1535365#post1535365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An examination of the dangers of powers and hubris is certainly something that is possible in Mage. The game, however, does not adhere entirely to that framework</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's one of the biggest double-edged aspects of the WoD:<br /> <br /> The games are bad at sticking to their core premises This is great if you want to explore all the other ways you can play the games, and it sucks if you're trying to stick to the core premises and the game keeps going off on other tangents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-10T11:55:51-07:00","id":1535417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1535368#post1535368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book of Secrets is but one of many books where the author directly states it: make no mistake, Mages are monsters.<br /> <br /> What happens is that the game, as all other games in WoD, has many themes to explore, and angst about your own monstrosity isn't the main one by far.<br /> <br /> Angst for being a monster isn't particularly important (but still possible) in any line but Vampire. Yet Werewolves take lives almost as an afterthought, fairies are emotional vampires at best and serial kidnappers with some frequency, your best Demon is a cult leader with all that entails. They're monster, inevitably, all of them.<br /> <br /> Mages aren't simply enacting miracles. They're raping reality with the stated goal of making it what they think it should be, without any concern for what other people want or need it to be.<br /> <br /> They bend and break rules, abuse minds and destinies, they trash around as they see fit. And the common people can't do shit about it, they're stripped of any right to interject or adequately resist, they're robbed of any sense of safety on even the most basic expectations on how the very reality around them should work.<br /> <br /> It is true to the game even if it isn't a focus or theme, which is another thing entirely. You shouldn't play Mage ruminating how despicable your nature is. But while your character may never see it that way, they're monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure if Book of Secrets is the best example, as it was explicitly part of the Mage 20th anniversary line. Earlier editions of Mage did not really stick to a clear vision of what mages were supposed to really be. For example, in 1e, mages of the Traditions are explicitly portrayed as being more virtuous than mages of the Technocracy, even though they are also depicted as being quite disconnected from the rest of humanity. <br /> <br /> Also, it is not really possible to depict mages as monsters without also necessarily implying that various miracle-workers throughout history were monsters. There have certainly been criticisms of religious figures and charismatic leaders in literature, such as in Dune, but Mage as a whole does not adhere solely to that criticism. Essentially, in order for mages to be monsters, having a obsessive, strong conviction for a particular ideology has to be inherently monstrous, and I am not sure if that is something that the writers ever really stated. <br /> <br /> In the setting, Sleepers have Avatars just as much as mages do. If mages are monsters, then all of humanity are also monsters in some capacity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-10T12:07:28-07:00","id":1535418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1535373#post1535373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's one of the biggest double-edged aspects of the WoD:<br /> <br /> The games are bad at sticking to their core premises This is great if you want to explore all the other ways you can play the games, and it sucks if you're trying to stick to the core premises and the game keeps going off on other tangents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see what you mean. I think that the Chronicles of Darkness games kept the themes of each game more focused than the old World of Darkness games did. That being said, the theme of hubris was always leavened by the fact that mages were able to avoid the dangers of hubris and attain Ascension. There are certainly works which focus more on power corrupting absolutely, but that is not the theme which many of the editions of Mage went for. Corruption was presented as a possibility and a real danger, but a path towards Ascension was also displayed as well. Mage specifically permits the idea that mages really are right and justified. One does not need to assume it, but that is a possibility that is not inherently discounted by the premise of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-10T17:18:25-07:00","id":1535424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1535417#post1535417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure if Book of Secrets is the best example, as it was explicitly part of the Mage 20th anniversary line. Earlier editions of Mage did not really stick to a clear vision of what mages were supposed to really be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, Brucato, the lead developer of M20, was also the lead on 2e, and wrote on a large number of the 1e books. There is basically no developer or writer that has output more words in official Mage: the Ascension books than him. He was the choice to make M20 precisely because he was considered one of the only people that could make a game that would bridge the massive divide between 1e/2e fans and Rev. fans after Revised did a bunch of unpopular changes (because he actually set up a lot of them in the late 2e metaplot, so he knew how to deal with them without making the Revised fans feel wrong for liking them).<br /> <br /> I understand the appeal to authority here has it's weaknesses, but there basically is no stronger authority on the subject regardless of what edition the quote came from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, in 1e, mages of the Traditions are explicitly portrayed as being more virtuous than mages of the Technocracy, even though they are also depicted as being quite disconnected from the rest of humanity. </div> </div> </div>Being more virtuous than the 1e Technocracy is a very low bar. The 1e Camarilla is more virtuous than the 1e Sabbat, that doesn't make the Camrilla an organization of good people.<br /> <br /> The Traditions have never been just &quot;disconnected&quot; they've always wanted an active role in human society to their own purposes. While the future the Traditions envision might be more appealing (or at least was in the 90s, the messaging in Mage has aged poorly) than the Technocracy, that doesn't mean it's actually good for Sleepers. Sleepers side with the Technocracy without realizing it because the Technocracy talks a much better game about make the lives of everyday folks better instead of working for a world where social status is dictated by mystic enlightenment (even if the Union is a totalitarian organization that expects the masses to conform for their pittances of safety and comfort, and the Traditions are open about an uneven society, but a society where people are free to achieve as much as they can or want to work for).<br /> <br /> I mean, the 1e Euthanatos being members of the Traditions says plenty about the moral standing of the organization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it is not really possible to depict mages as monsters without also necessarily implying that various miracle-workers throughout history were monsters. </div> </div> </div>Who said any of those figures were mages? True Faith and Numina allow for &quot;miracle&quot; workers that aren't mages.<br /> <br /> Also... the whole WoD is about monsters that have a moral/sympathetic hook that makes them interesting to play rather than being irredeemable scum that should be put down. Werewolves are monsters, but they do plenty of good things (including claiming responsibility for being some historical miracle workers of their own).<br /> <br /> So yes, any mage miracle worker was a monster. Just a monster that did enough good things they went down in mythology as a positive figure despite anything else they did.<br /> <br /> Also... a lot of older mythology doesn't treat this as a black &amp; white moral issue. World mythologies are full of flawed heroes that did some pretty nasty things as well as some great good things. The need to treat mythological figures as either the purest of saints or the darkest of sinners is a relatively new thing since perfect flat moral characters are hard to relate to; where complex moral figures that mess up and do bad things to are things people can related to and feel inspired to do well since they're not idealizing perfect.<br /> <br /> That doesn't even get into one person's saint is another person's monster. Vlad Tepes III aka Dracula himself, is a perfect example of someone that is both a folk hero and champion of Christian values and faith, and a fiendish monster than tortured his enemies and took great joy in impaling people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Essentially, in order for mages to be monsters, having a obsessive, strong conviction for a particular ideology has to be inherently monstrous, and I am not sure if that is something that the writers ever really stated. </div> </div> </div>Um, you just had this quoted from the books at you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the setting, Sleepers have Avatars just as much as mages do. If mages are monsters, then all of humanity are also monsters in some capacity. </div> </div> </div>Yep. That's the point. Every human has the seed of monstrosity in them. Most people are never placed in the position of having the power to truly impact the future of the world, and the few that are, are rarely the people you'd wish they would be.<br /> <br /> The WoD has never been a game that holds up humans as an inherently good thing. The monsters of the WoD are metaphors for how readily we accept monstrosity in our world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1535418#post1535418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That being said, the theme of hubris was always leavened by the fact that mages were able to avoid the dangers of hubris and attain Ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>How many characters in the setting are objectively known to have achieved Ascension? Which faction even knows how to do it in theory (not just accepts it as a concept)? How many mages have done truly horrible things in their pursuit of their personal view of Ascension?<br /> <br /> Vampire has Golconda too. Wraith has Transcendence. These &quot;win&quot; states exist in the games are vague, poorly defined, nearly impossible to achieve (if the books even state how), and are in-universe myth more than fact for most members of these groups. Even if we accept that Ascension is possible, most mages don't really think they'll ever get there if it is, because they've never seen it happen, and mages see a lot of crazy shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but a path towards Ascension was also displayed as well. </div> </div> </div>Which book actually details what it takes to achieve Ascension instead of just states that it might be possible?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mage specifically permits the idea that mages really are right and justified. One does not need to assume it, but that is a possibility that is not inherently discounted by the premise of the game. </div> </div> </div>Mage is not unique here. The Garou have a much stronger argument for being right and justified in their actions... and nobody holds them up as not-monsters out-of-character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-10T17:52:00-07:00","id":1535425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1535417#post1535417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, in 1e, mages of the Traditions are explicitly portrayed as being more virtuous than mages of the Technocracy, even though they are also depicted as being quite disconnected from the rest of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e Mages actively fight for a world without any form of modern safe technology. Most of them literally want to go back to the Middle Ages and bring the world with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it is not really possible to depict mages as monsters without also necessarily implying that various miracle-workers throughout history were monsters. </div> </div> </div>It is not about having powers. It is about being able to change reality on a whim.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Essentially, in order for mages to be monsters, having a obsessive, strong conviction for a particular ideology has to be inherently monstrous </div> </div> </div>Having an <u><b>obsessive</b></u> conviction most definitely makes one a monster to begin with. You just have to add power to their obsession, and Mage does so in spades.<br /> <br /> You're still missing the point about theme, about the distinction between an aspect of the character and the focus of the narrative. You keep bringing narrative flavor over and over as proof of something it doesn't prove.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-10T18:51:40-07:00","id":1535426,"title":"","content":"Being a monster doesn't mean you're evil. The term originally referred to anything strange or unusual, and while it's adopted a degree of moral judgment, a monster is still someone who is strange and terrifying. There's plenty of stories about strange and terrifying monsters who are nevertheless outright benevolent, sometimes even moreso than the normal people around them. Some of the supernaturals in World of Darkness could quite easily fall into this category. The fact that the mage is outright benevolent and heroically fighting against a totalitarian force doesn't change that the mage is able to casually violate &quot;the rules&quot; of reality. The fact that the Garou is trying to stop a force of cosmic corruption doesn't change the fact that they're an inherently terrifying creature who turns into a giant furry blender.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-10T20:46:59-07:00","id":1535428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1535426#post1535426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a monster doesn't mean you're evil. The term originally referred to anything strange or unusual, and while it's adopted a degree of moral judgment, a monster is still someone who is strange and terrifying. There's plenty of stories about strange and terrifying monsters who are nevertheless outright benevolent, sometimes even moreso than the normal people around them. Some of the supernaturals in World of Darkness could quite easily fall into this category. The fact that the mage is outright benevolent and heroically fighting against a totalitarian force doesn't change that the mage is able to casually violate &quot;the rules&quot; of reality. The fact that the Garou is trying to stop a force of cosmic corruption doesn't change the fact that they're an inherently terrifying creature who turns into a giant furry blender.</div> </div> </div> </div>Siberakh Zangief: &quot;Just because you are a monster doesn't mean that you are a *monster*.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T09:38:05-07:00","id":1535442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1535426#post1535426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a monster doesn't mean you're evil. The term originally referred to anything strange or unusual, and while it's adopted a degree of moral judgment, a monster is still someone who is strange and terrifying. There's plenty of stories about strange and terrifying monsters who are nevertheless outright benevolent, sometimes even moreso than the normal people around them. Some of the supernaturals in World of Darkness could quite easily fall into this category. The fact that the mage is outright benevolent and heroically fighting against a totalitarian force doesn't change that the mage is able to casually violate &quot;the rules&quot; of reality. The fact that the Garou is trying to stop a force of cosmic corruption doesn't change the fact that they're an inherently terrifying creature who turns into a giant furry blender.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that's true, the splats are also still monsters in the sense that they are extremely harmful either to those who live near them or to people they meet casually. For Mages, it's the terrible combination of obsession with power.<br /> <br /> It surely doesn't mean they want to be bad, or that they can't try to minimize the harm, and even sometimes make amends by improving the world in some way (although that's still a complicated proposition when you're dealing with an obsessive idealist).<br /> <br /> But regardless if they achieve a net positive, they still cause a lot of harm as an extension of their nature, of how easy and even necessary it is for them to casually destroy lives, even without notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T11:21:31-07:00","id":1535448,"title":"","content":"CofD for me certainly makes the system integration of the setting way better than WoD ever did.<br /> <br /> But even more so than that, CofD also made those core power scale for every supernatural (like blood potency, gnosis, essence...). Which gave the possibility for players characters to rise in power generally, BUT the banes related to each supernatural also rose with it. So, I believe CofD tends to be less power-centric, although you can be more powerful, and yet it makes being powerful more monstrous also. <br /> <br /> While I think CofD mechanically many times gets way too crunchy and heavy for my taste, in terms of sophistication, versatility and thematic resonance it knocks it out of the park. For me, they make vamps, weries, changles, and mummos so much more interesting!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T14:30:29-07:00","id":1535464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1535442#post1535442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While that's true, the splats are also still monsters in the sense that they are extremely harmful either to those who live near them or to people they meet casually. For Mages, it's the terrible combination of obsession with power.<br /> <br /> It surely doesn't mean they want to be bad, or that they can't try to minimize the harm, and even sometimes make amends by improving the world in some way (although that's still a complicated proposition when you're dealing with an obsessive idealist).<br /> <br /> But regardless if they achieve a net positive, they still cause a lot of harm as an extension of their nature, of how easy and even necessary it is for them to casually destroy lives, even without notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is true for any splat. No, not even vampires. In some cases they are a complete positive for the community. For every splat there are members it's true for, but it's also true that some humans are extremely harmful to those who live near them or those they meet casually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T16:11:14-07:00","id":1535466,"title":"","content":"While True Faith is fairly potent, there are definite limits to the other forms of Numina. In order to model levitation for example, you are going to need something stronger than hedge magic. That being said, psychic phenomena could also be used to model levitation, though Numina in general have definite limits. Furthermore, the idea that mages as a construct are something that can entirely be disconnected from history does not align with the presentation that the books use. Many of the Traditions and Crafts are plainly based upon a variety of normal magical traditions. The Spheres can explicitly accomplish many miraculous effects that are greater in potency than hedge magic. Awakenings hold many parallels with certain varieties of mystical experiences and peak experiences. It is somewhat disingenuous to claim that the mages do not align with the image of the miracle-worker.<br /> <br /> Also, you seem to sort of acknowledge the more positive framing of mages in past editions when you said that the messaging of the earlier editions of Mage had aged poorly. The Traditions were originally written in a more appealing manner. Whether or not that was a bad thing or a good thing can be debated.<br /> <br /> Finally, I would not necessarily say that having an obsessive conviction regarding something necessarily renders one a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T16:11:14-07:00","id":1535467,"title":"","content":"While True Faith is fairly potent, there are definite limits to the other forms of Numina. In order to model levitation for example, you are going to need something stronger than hedge magic. That being said, psychic phenomena could also be used to model levitation, though Numina in general have definite limits. Furthermore, the idea that mages as a construct are something that can entirely be disconnected from history does not align with the presentation that the books use. Many of the Traditions and Crafts are plainly based upon a variety of normal magical traditions. The Spheres can explicitly accomplish many miraculous effects that are greater in potency than hedge magic. Awakenings hold many parallels with certain varieties of mystical experiences and peak experiences. It is somewhat disingenuous to claim that the mages do not align with the image of the miracle-worker.<br /> <br /> Also, you seem to sort of acknowledge the more positive framing of mages in past editions when you said that the messaging of the earlier editions of Mage had aged poorly. The Traditions were originally written in a more appealing manner. Whether or not that was a bad thing or a good thing can be debated.<br /> <br /> Finally, I would not necessarily say that having an obsessive conviction regarding something necessarily renders one a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T18:44:16-07:00","id":1535475,"title":"","content":"On the fantasy-side? Hmmm, maybe. I know that in CoD, healing's faster than in OWoD. I feel that celerity, took a step-down, though, I like what they did with it. I like the varying degrees of damage for sunlight/sliver based off of humanity and harmony. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1534443#post1534443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .game of Power Armor in Cyberpunk 2020, a game with a BattleTech RPG in the Deep Periphery with no major state assistance vs one closer to the Succession Wars, or the difference between Forsaken and Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ACPAs are overrated; I can say that, given Night's Edge, V:tM was more powerful, but, the psconic-powers did make a sort of difference in CP2020.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T18:52:34-07:00","id":1535477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1534441-is-world-of-darkness-is-a-bit-more-of-a-power-fantasy-than-cofd?p=1535475#post1535475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ACPAs are overrated; I can say that, given Night's Edge, V:tM was more powerful, but, the psconic-powers did make a sort of difference in CP2020.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just sub in larger vehicles with more impressive armament, then. I'm fairly certain that the point still stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}